WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.137
Tester: Hello. This is the home page of Marcelo Paiva's site, in Safari, with VoiceOver on.

2
00:00:06.137 --> 00:00:11.475
Tester: I'm the tester. I'll drive VoiceOver and the keyboard, and tell you what I hear.

3
00:00:11.876 --> 00:00:13.161
Reviewer: And I'm the reviewer.

4
00:00:13.161 --> 00:00:17.322
Reviewer: When something sounds wrong, I'll name the guideline it falls under,

5
00:00:17.322 --> 00:00:20.381
Reviewer: and explain why it matters to the person it stops.

6
00:00:20.381 --> 00:00:23.502
Reviewer: When it's fixed, I'll say what changed in the code.

7
00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:28.266
VoiceOver: Marcelo Paiva — Design Engineer web content is in the VoiceOver cursor

8
00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:29.488
Tester: The goal is simple.

9
00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:33.992
Tester: Can someone using VoiceOver understand this page, find what they need,

10
00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:36.566
Tester: and use its controls, without seeing it?

11
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.119
Reviewer: This is a first pass, before testing with people with disabilities.

12
00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:43.968
Reviewer: It finds problems early, so they can be fixed,

13
00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:47.870
Reviewer: and so the time with people goes on what only they can tell us.

14
00:00:48.272 --> 00:00:52.943
Tester: I test in six steps. First, I inspect the page structure in the code.

15
00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:55.110
Tester: Second, the keyboard on its own.

16
00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.172
Tester: Third, a reading pass with the screen reader, top to bottom.

17
00:00:59.172 --> 00:01:04.656
Tester: Fourth, jumping by headings, landmarks and links. Fifth, the controls themselves.

18
00:01:04.656 --> 00:01:07.296
Tester: And sixth, real tasks, start to finish.

19
00:01:07.698 --> 00:01:09.962
Reviewer: Each step gets its own short video.

20
00:01:09.962 --> 00:01:14.360
Reviewer: When we find a problem, we fix it, and test again in the same video.

21
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.047
Reviewer: At the end, we list what still needs testing with people.
